-- each signal, raised and waited for
Interrupt Terminate Hangup Quit User1 User2 Pipe Child 
-- deliveries of one signal while it waits are one
wait: User1
then: nothing
-- signals that wait together come in the order of Signal
Interrupt Hangup Quit User2 
-- nothing arrives
wait_timeout of 30 ms: nothing
it lasted at least that long: true
wait_timeout of nothing: nothing
try_next: nothing
wait_timeout of 10 s after a raise: Terminate
-- a child that ends
wait_timeout of 10 s: Child
-- an ignored signal does nothing
the program goes on
-- a Signals gives back the disposition it found
caught while held: User2
ignored again once the Signals is gone
-- and forgets what it had recorded
a new Signals starts with: nothing
and catches what is raised now: User1
reset of a signal that is not held is accepted
